From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:25:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 118/119] fix: the preview gate's "log only on a change" logged
 every frame

The gate remembered ONE (verdict, pipeline name) pair, but a routine editor session
runs six to ten pipelines and SetSceneReferredPipelineGate() is called once for each
of them, every frame. Every call therefore invalidated the pair the previous call had
just stored, so the change test was true every time and the console filled with

  [SceneReferred] pipeline 'Minimum_1' scene-referred: no (no display transform ...)
  [SceneReferred] pipeline 'Standard_0' scene-referred: yes (owns a display transform)

twice per frame while Scene Referred was on, burying every other line.

The remembered verdict becomes per pipeline, keyed by name, so the alternation between
pipelines is no longer a change and each pipeline prints once - and again only when ITS
own answer moves. The reason string is part of the key, not decoration: 'Standard_0'
going from "owns a display transform" to "map screenshot - an asset, not a picture" is
the same verdict for a different cause and is worth the line. Wording unchanged.

Turning the switch off now prints one line and forgets every verdict, so the next time
it comes on the user gets the full roll call again instead of silence left over from
the previous session.

Audited every other [SceneReferred] log line for the same shape. The format-reformat
lines, "request flipped", the inert LDR post stage, the light-unit convention and the
LUT loads are all latched per instance and were already once-per-change. One was not:
the metering histogram's creation failure is retried every frame the meter runs, so it
is latched too, and cleared when a target is finally created.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
